    "field": "Biogenic volatile organic compound emissions",
    "problem": "Previous comprehensive books on tree volatile organic compound (BVOC) emissions are outdated, and the vast, fragmented biological knowledge accumulated since their publication has not been systematically synthesized, creating significant uncertainties in current predictive models and inventories of emissions and their atmospheric impacts.",
    "method": "This document is a book that reviews and synthesizes existing knowledge on tree volatile organic compound emissions; it does not propose a single, specific method to solve a problem.",
    "task": "This book's task is to synthesize the current understanding of the biology, environmental controls, and predictive modeling of volatile organic compound emissions from trees, covering scales from molecular mechanisms to global atmospheric impacts.",
